  "case_id": "2023-22-1025",
  "decision": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9016fb98b486b0441440a16b7b11759b90cc6566bac3ebbc7554720ed0a54a4d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9016fb98b486-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court vacated the lower court\u2019s judgment and remanded for proceedings consistent with this opinion."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9016fb98b486b0441440a16b7b11759b90cc6566bac3ebbc7554720ed0a54a4d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9016fb98b486-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 15,
              "start": 15
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Alito, in his concurrence, Justice Alito wrote that a plaintiff must provide objective evidence to satisfy the Nieves exception."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9016fb98b486b0441440a16b7b11759b90cc6566bac3ebbc7554720ed0a54a4d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9016fb98b486-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 16,
              "start": 16
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Alito, in his concurrence, Justice Alito added that evidence showing the plaintiff\u2019s speech was a \u201csubstantial or motivating factor\u201d should not be considered unless the plaintiff provides other evidence to satisfy the Nieves exception."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9016fb98b486b0441440a16b7b11759b90cc6566bac3ebbc7554720ed0a54a4d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9016fb98b486-0001-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Alito, in his concurrence, Justice Alito stated that a plaintiff must prove there was no probable cause for the charge, rejecting any analogy to abuse of process."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9016fb98b486b0441440a16b7b11759b90cc6566bac3ebbc7554720ed0a54a4d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9016fb98b486-0001-0007"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 22,
              "start": 22
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "In his concurrence, Justice Kavanaugh warned that a \u201csplit\u2011second\u201d rule would create a perverse incentive for police officers to make quick arrests rather than deliberate ones."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9016fb98b486b0441440a16b7b11759b90cc6566bac3ebbc7554720ed0a54a4d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9016fb98b486-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "In her concurrence, Justice Jackson warned that the Court should foreclose Gonzalez\u2019s attempt to contest her mens rea for the \u00a7\u202f1983 retaliatory\u2011arrest claim and noted that an objectively reasonable officer would have known the plaintiff\u2019s conduct was accidental."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9016fb98b486b0441440a16b7b11759b90cc6566bac3ebbc7554720ed0a54a4d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9016fb98b486-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 26,
              "start": 26
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "9016fb98b486b0441440a16b7b11759b90cc6566bac3ebbc7554720ed0a54a4d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9016fb98b486-0002-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 27,
              "start": 27
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "In his dissent, Justice Thomas argued that the Nieves exception requires objective evidence and that an abuse\u2011of\u2011process claim is not analogous to Gonzalez\u2019s retaliatory\u2011arrest claim."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9016fb98b486b0441440a16b7b11759b90cc6566bac3ebbc7554720ed0a54a4d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9016fb98b486-0002-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 28,
              "start": 28
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "In his dissent, Justice Thomas further contended that Gonzalez\u2019s central argument is that her arrest was invalid because the defendants had an improper motive."
      }
    ],
